 expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Idaho remains one of the most Republican states in presidential politics, and the 2028 open-seat race does little to change that. With the incumbent term-limited, both parties enter without a settled nominee, and no Idaho-specific general-election polls or expert ratings are available. The state's R+18 partisan lean is the dominant fact: Democrats have not carried Idaho since 1964, and Republican margins have held up even in strong Democratic years nationally.\n\nNational headlines show Trump's approval underwater across most states, and the 2028 primary fields on both sides remain unsettled, with figures like Harris, Newsom, Vance, and Rubio mentioned. None of that points to a competitive general election in Idaho itself. The forecast expects a comfortable Republican win in the mid-to-high teens, with the remaining uncertainty reflecting the absence of local polling rather than any sign of a genuine contest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0246, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0537, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0553, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0476, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0546, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0466, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0509, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.049, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -18.0}]}